{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["What are your result types, and what will each person do with theirs? Write the four results before you edit the questions.","Does every answer option feel like something a reasonable person might pick, with no option that reads as the wrong one?","What will the emailed profile contain, and is it worth an email address to the player?","Is this for fun on social media, a team workshop, or a hiring event? The tone of the results should match."],"howToUseResponses":"Count how many people land in each type: if nearly everyone gets the same result, move the score bands or rewrite the questions that everyone answers the same way. Compare the self-guess with the actual result for a fun follow-up post. Send each email subscriber content that suits their type, and use the spread of types in a team session to talk about how people like to work.","customizeSteps":["Decide your own types first, then rewrite each question so its answers run from one end of your scale to the other, scored 3 down to 0.","Rename the four results and adjust the score bands so each type is reachable, then take the quiz a few times with different answers to check.","Change what the email question promises, then share the link on social media or embed the quiz on a landing page."],"faqs":[{"q":"How do you make a personality quiz?","a":"Start with the results, then write questions where each answer points toward one of them. Keep every option believable, so nobody feels there is a wrong answer."},{"q":"How does this personality quiz decide the result?","a":"Each answer carries between 0 and 3 points, from improviser to planner. The total out of 18 picks one of four types, and you can move the thresholds."},{"q":"Is this a scientific personality test?","a":"No. It is a light, fun quiz about everyday habits. Say so in your greeting if you use it at work, so nobody takes the result too seriously."},{"q":"Can a personality quiz help me collect leads?","a":"Yes. People like sharing their type, and offering a longer profile by email gives them a real reason to leave their address."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":10,"title":"Work style personality quiz","description":"Six everyday scenarios that place people on a planner to improviser scale, with four result types.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_personal00","ref":"welcome","title":"Do you plan the week on Sunday or decide on Monday morning? Answer six everyday situations to find your work style.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_personal01","ref":"first_name","title":"Whose work style are we reading today?","description":"A first name is plenty.","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique":false,"minLength":0,"maxLength":40},{"id":"blk_personal02","ref":"saturday","title":"A free Saturday opens up. What happens?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_it_s_planned","label":"It's planned by Friday night","image_key":null,"score":3},{"id":"opt_i_jot_down","label":"I jot down a loose list","image_key":null,"score":2},{"id":"opt_i_pick_one","label":"I pick one thing and see where it goes","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_i_wake_up","label":"I wake up and decide","image_key":null,"score":0}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_personal03","ref":"new_project","title":"You're handed a new project. What's your first move?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_write_out_every","label":"Write out every step and a timeline","image_key":null,"score":3},{"id":"opt_sketch_the_big","label":"Sketch the big milestones","image_key":null,"score":2},{"id":"opt_start_on_the","label":"Start on the part that excites me","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_dive_in_and","label":"Dive in and work it out as I go","image_key":null,"score":0}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_personal04","ref":"plans_change","title":"Plans change at the last minute. How do you feel?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_thrown_until_i","label":"Thrown, until I have a new plan","image_key":null,"score":3},{"id":"opt_a_little_annoyed","label":"A little annoyed, then I adjust","image_key":null,"score":2},{"id":"opt_fine_it_happens","label":"Fine, it happens","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_quietly_pleased_something","label":"Quietly pleased, something new","image_key":null,"score":0}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_personal05","ref":"desk","title":"Be honest: what does your desk or inbox look like right now?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_sorted_into_folders","label":"Sorted into folders","image_key":null,"score":3},{"id":"opt_mostly_tidy","label":"Mostly tidy","image_key":null,"score":2},{"id":"opt_organised_chaos","label":"Organised chaos","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_best_not_to","label":"Best not to ask","image_key":null,"score":0}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_personal06","ref":"packing","title":"How do you pack for a trip?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_from_a_checklist","label":"From a checklist, days ahead","image_key":null,"score":3},{"id":"opt_the_night_before","label":"The night before, from memory","image_key":null,"score":2},{"id":"opt_an_hour_before","label":"An hour before I leave","image_key":null,"score":1},{"id":"opt_i_ll_buy","label":"I'll buy whatever I forget","image_key":null,"score":0}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_personal07","ref":"deadlines","title":"Which sounds most like you and deadlines?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"